    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe identity key was redesigned to `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`, and duplicate detection was consolidated onto it.\n\n**`mapper/Soundex.java`** (new) \u2014 American Soundex coder as a standalone utility. This location matters: I first put `soundex` as a `static` method on the `OwnerMapper` interface, but MapStruct adopted the `String \u2192 String` helper as an *implicit property-mapping method* and ran every string field (telephone, email, \u2026) through it, producing empty telephones and a 500 at persist time. Moving it out of the mapper fixed that.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `identityKey(owner)` now returns the full lower-case hex SHA-256 of `telephone|email|Soundex.of(lastName)` (was the plaintext `telephone|email|householdId`). `householdId` is untouched since it still feeds `householdSize` and the membership-level cap.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Duplicate detection (409) now compares the single `identityKey`, still filtering out `deleted` owners. The email-domain blocklist still runs first (in `normalizeEmail`, before this check).\n- Removed the separate household-duplicate 409 block (the `householdId`-based `contactCollides` rejection) and the now-unused `identityContact` helper. Two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones now have distinct keys, so they're created rather than rejected.\n- `findPossibleDuplicate` now soft-matches when the identity key **differs** but `Soundex.of(lastName)` and postcode both match \u2014 so the telephone-differing pair above is flagged `possibleDuplicate`. A declared `sharesHousehold` member with a soft match is still not flagged.\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `identityKey` doc/example to describe the 64-hex SHA-256 form.\n\nTests: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS. `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` confirms the 64-char lowercase-hex shape and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` confirms an identical identity still yields 409.",
